title: ConsentFix: sign-in code pasted back to the page
severity: critical
score: 75
tags: consent-phishing, clickfix, aitm
attack: T1528, T1566.002, T1204.004
description: A non-Microsoft page shows a real Entra authorize URL for a first-party (pre-
  consented) app, such as Azure CLI, with a localhost redirect_uri. The page tells the
  visitor to paste the resulting URL or code into a box on that page. The attacker gets
  the authorization code (ConsentFix / AuthCodeFix). A page that only describes the step
  (a tutorial) gets the medium rule. Tenant check: Microsoft's tenant
  f8cdef31-a31e-4b4a-93e4-5f571e91255a owns the service principal of a first-party app.
---
// A first-party app's authorize URL with a loopback redirect on a foreign page
// (see firstparty_loopback_authorize in _shared.kql) ...
firstparty_loopback_authorize
// ... on a page that asks the visitor to paste a URL back into a text box.
| where exists(paste_back_frames)
